# Full Throttle: "After this main phase, there are two additional combat phases" does nothing when the spell resolves outside a main
# phase (CR 500.8), and "at the beginning of each combat this turn" lasts only this turn (CR 603.7b). Brazen Bluff lets Bot1 cast it free
# during combat on turn 3, after Fanatical Firebrand attacked: no combat follows, so the Firebrand stays tapped (nothing untaps it), the
# turn goes from the postcombat main straight to the end step, and the delayed trigger is gone when turn 4 begins (Delayed.Count 1 -> 0).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Fanatical Firebrand
Full Throttle
Brazen Bluff
Sol Ring
Mountain
Mountain x24

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Opt
Island x28

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Fanatical Firebrand.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Fanatical Firebrand)
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Opt.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Brazen Bluff.Cast(Opt)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Decline
Bot1.Choose(Full Throttle)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Fanatical Firebrand.Tapped = true
? Delayed.Count = 1
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Step = End
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Delayed.Count = 0

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield.Fanatical Firebrand.Tapped = true
Bot1.Graveyard = Full Throttle; Brazen Bluff; Black Lotus
